 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Krüger and Westermann in 2003 as an efficient way to perform volume raycasting on GPUs by leveraging rasterization [S1, unofficial][S3]. It was developed as an alternative to procedural ray-box intersection, which placed a heavy load on fragment shaders [S1, unofficial]. The technique has been widely adopted in GPU-based volume rendering pipelines, particularly in early implementations of real-time raycasting [S1, unofficial][S3]. It is often used in conjunction with early ray termination and empty space skipping to further optimize performance [S1, unofficial].
